 184: ## 22. 2026-11-09: oracle-gains construction (Volume 2 fix or Volume 4 limit?)
 185: 
 186: Question recorded before running: can any setting of the 2,096 mask gains inside the rule's bounds [0.2, 1.8] make a safe non-king capture the top choice on a development board? Construction: repeatedly set each gain to the bound that favours the best safe capture over its top rival (by their per-edge presynaptic KC rates), then rank exactly. Not learning; an upper-bound construction for these synapses. If it fails, no rule acting only on these synapses can pass that board (a finite Volume 4 measurement); if it succeeds, the limit is the rule or the teaching, which points to a Volume 2 fix.
 187: - **Oracle-gains result** (`runs/fly-connections-memory-2026-11-08/oracle-gains-probe-v1.log`, both drive levels, 3 dev boards, 6 iterations): **never solved.** Each step sets 455-2,090 of the 2,096 gains to a bound in favour of the best safe capture over its current top rival; a second rival then overtakes, and the construction cycles between two gain settings. Closest: board 5XRGyGSj:13 at zero drive, margin -1.5e-8 (start -1.6e-6). Default drive: margins stay -1.2e-6 to -1.1e-5. Limit: greedy single-rival construction, not an exhaustive search; strong evidence, not a proof that no gain setting works. A proof needs the multi-rival bound (for example a linearized program over all rivals, then exact verification).
