documentation/design/neural-learning/fly-connections-memory-v1-revision-4-2026-11-09.md:28:Plastic connections = the 8 "DAN ⊸ MBON" rows of Table 1 (for example dat⊸sav, cat⊸rav, cat⊸mat, cav⊸rat, fat⊸mav, fav⊸mat, and the remaining rows transcribed exactly at build). Each connection's mask = existing positive-sign KC edges onto that MBON's cells; each uses its own DAN population's actual endpoint rate in the unchanged ReversalMemory rule (eta 0.5, gains [0.2, 1.8], activity scale 1.5). An MBON receiving two DAN rows gets one gain per (edge, DAN row), combined multiplicatively. **Open:** the exact equation by which the paper combines several DANs on one compartment; if the paper sums dopamine factors instead, follow it.
